WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.866
On the “Documents & service”

2
00:00:01.866 --> 00:00:03.700
tab, press “Upload document”:

3
00:00:03.759 --> 00:00:04.746
“Choose file”

4
00:00:04.746 --> 00:00:07.531
or “Take photo”, a title and a category.

5
00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:10.876
If it is an update, file it as a “New version of”

6
00:00:10.876 --> 00:00:15.739
an older one, and mark medical or sensitive files “Restricted”.

7
00:00:16.839 --> 00:00:19.764
Files up to twenty MB are stored on this device,

8
00:00:19.892 --> 00:00:22.005
and on your sync server if connected.

9
00:00:22.307 --> 00:00:23.804
Text is read locally.

10
00:00:23.991 --> 00:00:25.952
In “Review extracted values”

11
00:00:25.976 --> 00:00:28.854
you accept, correct or reject each value,

12
00:00:28.913 --> 00:00:32.732
and nothing is written until you press “Apply accepted values”.

13
00:00:33.832 --> 00:00:36.525
To have it signed, press “Send for signature”:

14
00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:39.857
you choose the document, the language, a title,

15
00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:43.200
the client’s e-mail and how many days the link is valid.

16
00:00:43.445 --> 00:00:48.471
The client reads the PDF, confirms with a six-digit code sent by e-mail,

17
00:00:48.658 --> 00:00:51.350
and signs with a finger or the mouse.

18
00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:56.327
It is a simple electronic signature under the eIDAS regulation,

19
00:00:56.513 --> 00:00:58.927
and an audit page is added to the document.

20
00:00:59.393 --> 00:01:01.133
Under “Electronic signatures”

21
00:01:01.157 --> 00:01:02.760
you see when it was sent and when it

22
00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:05.615
was signed, and “Add to documents”

23
00:01:05.615 --> 00:01:08.807
puts the signed PDF in the client’s documents.

24
00:01:09.907 --> 00:01:12.483
And if a document looks like a policy schedule,

25
00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:17.720
the CRM suggests creating the policy from it, checking the values first.

26
00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:20.038
In the next lesson:

27
00:01:20.097 --> 00:01:22.453
reports and the picture of your business.
